Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 01:16:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): Tavily come secondo livello di web_search / Tavily
 as second web_search tier
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

IT: nuovo TavilyWebProvider (packages/adapters/src/tavily-web.ts): POST
https://api.tavily.com/search con Authorization Bearer, search_depth "basic"
(1 credito per chiamata), max_results uguale al limite dello strumento;
results[] title/url/content mappati in {title, url, snippet} (solo http/https,
deduplicati). Con TAVILY_API_KEY impostata la catena diventa SearXNG → Tavily →
DuckDuckGo: Tavily viene chiamato solo se SearXNG va in errore, scade o non trova
nulla, e se anche Tavily fallisce o non trova nulla si ripiega su DuckDuckGo.
WEB_PROVIDER=tavily usa Tavily per primo. Timeout opzionale TAVILY_TIMEOUT_MS
(default 10 s). Ogni chiamata a Tavily viene registrata nel log («web_search
Tavily call», con esito, numero di risultati e durata, senza query né chiave),
così il consumo di crediti è visibile. web_fetch invariato. Test in
tavily-web.test.ts, compresa la catena completa.

EN: new TavilyWebProvider (packages/adapters/src/tavily-web.ts): POST
https://api.tavily.com/search with Bearer auth, search_depth "basic" (1 credit
per call), max_results equal to the tool cap; results[] title/url/content mapped
to {title, url, snippet} (http/https only, deduplicated). With TAVILY_API_KEY set
the chain becomes SearXNG → Tavily → DuckDuckGo: Tavily is only called when
SearXNG errors, times out or finds nothing, and when Tavily also fails or finds
nothing it falls back to DuckDuckGo. WEB_PROVIDER=tavily puts Tavily first.
Optional TAVILY_TIMEOUT_MS (default 10 s). Every Tavily call is logged ("web_search
Tavily call" with outcome, result count and duration, no query or key) so credit
use is visible. web_fetch unchanged. Tests in tavily-web.test.ts, including the
whole chain.
